<title>USA: Columbia Labs says Mexico clears Crinone.</title>
<headline>Columbia Labs says Mexico clears Crinone.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Columbia Laboratories Inc said Thursday Crinone, its vaginally delivered natural progesterone gel, has been cleared for marketing in Mexico.</p>
<p>Crinone was approved in Mexico for use in hormone replacement therapy, infertility treatments, premenstrual syndrome, secondary amenorrhea, dysmenorrhea and abnormal uterine bleeding.</p>
<p>As a result of this approval, Columbia will receive a $1 million milestone payment from Wyeth-Ayerst, a division of American Home Products Corp.</p>
<p>Crinone is being marketed by Wyeth-Ayerst.</p>
</text>
